{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01J5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(\\kappa(x)) \\to X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-points}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d830b8be08d2472d48fe658a95534b321228caa90b10a0fae5d1b980559d7e6e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57bbdf142ba605ad4ad9a9994f99ffb2eadbca24585197e632ec8807faa2cbd0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Points of <MATH_0002> correspond bijectively\nto equivalence classes of morphisms from spectra of\nfields into <MATH_0003>. Moreover, each equivalence class contains\na (unique up to unique isomorphism) smallest element\n<MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e8392151f502bed7b53bef170520a544f679c797629702acde6cf144dc6bfb4e", "unit_id": "tag:01J9:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01J5", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4ef0eb817ce8b3f6d725fa34b4c24447099996c35bc7e934b851b13e425bdf80", "source_text": "Follows from the discussion above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:67e40548dabe1674196d0ac35ee141ac83f45450399c3d21c79ce74a8a39c0c2", "unit_id": "tag:01J9:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01J5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(\\kappa(x)) \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(\\kappa(x')) \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(\\kappa(x')) \\to \\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$x'$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$x$", "MATH_0009": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(\\kappa(x)) \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\nX \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(\\kappa(s)) \\ar[r] &\n\\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_{S, s}) \\ar[r] &\nS.\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-specialize-points}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6ff33009e3e2e7dd2e69d0641b89e299c93c101efb27459d538351cb72808ceb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b468da2ad568f181304af9fc6bb080e0ca87e8eb3de44d39cc2036e0459c7f17", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOf course the morphisms <MATH_0001>\nfactor through the canonical morphisms\n<MATH_0002>.\nAnd the content of Lemma <REF_0001> is in\nthis setting that the morphism <MATH_0003>\nfactors as\n<MATH_0004>\nwhenever <MATH_0005> is a generalization of <MATH_0006>.\nIn case we have a morphism of schemes <MATH_0007>,\nand a point <MATH_0008> mapping to a point <MATH_0009> we obtain\na commutative diagram\n<MATH_0010>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c10a8121fe1bb190c185e2c11eb6f592d6f27598e0d792a89e61a8fecf4c2c22", "unit_id": "tag:01J5:prose-0004"}
